## AI-Assisted

## Isolates users' temporary and shm directories. Every login for a user will
## see the same variant of the directory, but different users will see
## different variants.
##
## https://www.kicksecure.com/wiki/Dev/Strong_Linux_User_Account_Isolation
## man namespace.conf

## FIXME: When elevating to root using `sudo`, the run-as-root process will see
## the calling user's variants of /tmp and friends, not the system instance.
## Maybe when logging in as root, use pam_namespace.so with the 'unmnt_only'
## argument?

/tmp       /run/pam-namespace/tmp-inst/   user:iscript=/usr/libexec/security-misc/pam-namespace-init   root
/var/tmp   /var/tmp/tmp-inst/             user   root
/dev/shm   /run/pam-namespace/shm-inst/   user   root
